WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
- Welcome back to the Kelly Clarkson Show!

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.742
I'm your guest host Sunita Mani.

00:00:05.742 --> 00:00:06.990
(crowd cheers)

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.740
Stepping in with my co-stars
from the new movie Spirited.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:15.003
Will Ferrell, Octavia
Spencer, and Ryan Reynolds.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.160
For people who don't know,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.800
the film is a fun spin
on a Christmas carol,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.630
but it's also a musical.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.480
Ryan, this was your first musical.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.680
Was it intimidating?

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.180
- Oh my God, it was so intimidating.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.460
I mean, it was singing
and dancing and I, I don't

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.380
think I've ever felt pressure and anxiety

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.174
like that on a movie, in my life.

00:00:33.174 --> 00:00:34.007
(crowd and costars laugh)

00:00:34.007 --> 00:00:34.840
That was intense.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:35.673
- Wow, you've done a lot of movies.

00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:37.080
- That was... I've done a lot of movies

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.390
and that was nothing, that
was nothing like this.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.170
We had dance, all of us had
dance camp for seven weeks.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.910
Seven or eight weeks,
and then, but before that

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.650
months of tap dance training

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.120
and vocal training and all kinds of stuff.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.040
So, I loved it 'cause I got insight into

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.000
what that world is like.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.060
I'm a huge fan of, of musicals,
but I, I've never done one.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.850
So, to have that privilege
to do this was pretty,

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:57.870
pretty exceptional. Yeah.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.010
- Definitely.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.060
Octavia.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.893
- [Octavia] Yes?

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.090
- I have to ask, there's a
lot of dancing in this movie

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:07.140
and you've posted your
dance skills on Instagram.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.810
- Oh, uh...

00:01:10.221 --> 00:01:11.115
- [Will] Oh, I did?

00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:12.585
- [Octavia] I, I, I did?

00:01:12.585 --> 00:01:13.418
- [Ryan] Who me?

00:01:13.418 --> 00:01:14.429
- [Sunita] Yeah.

00:01:14.429 --> 00:01:15.262
(crowd cheers)

00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:16.530
Oh yeah!

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.725
Oh, there it is and there you are.

00:01:18.725 --> 00:01:20.142
- [Ryan] Oh yeah.

00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:23.052
Love it.

00:01:23.052 --> 00:01:24.600
- Yeah. We, we, uh, and that's what

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.560
I'm doing in the movie, guys.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.180
- It's impressive.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.013
- No.

00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:30.240
- I mean did you have
formal training for that or?

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.073
- Not for that.

00:01:31.073 --> 00:01:34.470
For that, that was, that
was my impromptu like,

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.303
- You're a natural.

00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:36.136
- Ya know, crazy.

00:01:36.136 --> 00:01:36.969
- [Will] Yeah.

00:01:36.969 --> 00:01:38.387
- But

00:01:38.387 --> 00:01:40.170
can I, can I just say, and not about me?

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.010
About, talk about...

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.420
Oh yeah. Yeah.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.253
- [Ryan] Oh yeah.

00:01:43.253 --> 00:01:44.587
- See, you could all do that.

00:01:44.587 --> 00:01:45.420
- [Ryan] Crushin' it.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.253
- Right?

00:01:46.253 --> 00:01:48.510
She, you are amazing.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:49.410
You're an amazing dancer.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.014
- [Ryan] Born dancer right here,

00:01:51.014 --> 00:01:51.847
- Thank you, thank you.

00:01:51.847 --> 00:01:52.697
- [Ryan] And singer too.

00:01:52.697 --> 00:01:53.555
- Guys, thanks.

00:01:53.555 --> 00:01:55.093
I have a little dance in my background.

00:01:55.093 --> 00:01:55.926
- Amazing.

00:01:55.926 --> 00:01:56.759
- Amazing.

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:57.930
- Thank you.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.150
Will and Ryan, how would you rate your

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.280
dance skills in this movie?

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.830
- I, you know, we, well,
we tap, we had to tap,

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.320
which for both of us was terrifying.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.153
- Right.

00:02:08.153 --> 00:02:09.780
- I wouldn't say we
were like Fred Astaire.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.280
We were... I would say more like

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.840
Fred Astaire's lesser known brothers,

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:13.680
Greg and Percy.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.970
- Yeah.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.260
- Greg And Percy, a lot
of people don't know this,

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.875
they were born without bones.

00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:18.930
- [Sunita] I was a huge Percy fan.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.700
- And they couldn't dance

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.900
- Couldn't dance at all.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.720
But they taught Fred everything he knew.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.553
- [Ryan] Yeah.

00:02:25.553 --> 00:02:26.386
- Yeah.

00:02:26.386 --> 00:02:27.219
- The tap was the most terrifying for me.

00:02:27.219 --> 00:02:28.773
- Tap was, was terrifying.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.990
The other thing, and it
sounds simplistic to say,

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:36.624
but it's hard to sing and
dance at the same time.

00:02:36.624 --> 00:02:38.010
- At the same time.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.450
- Because you practice dancing,
then you practice singing,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.640
and then you're supposed to
combine them at some point.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.290
And you forget that you
have to combine them.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.130
- The worst.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.240
- Last question to everybody.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.883
Were you more comfortable
singing than dancing?

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.100
- I would say singing.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:53.933
- Singing.

00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:54.766
- I would say singing.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.320
That part felt really good. Yeah.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.652
- [Sunita] Yeah. Comes together.

00:02:59.652 --> 00:03:00.721
- What do you think?

00:03:00.721 --> 00:03:05.400
- You know, I, when you're
not used to any of it,

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.710
and you have a lot of eyes on you.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.690
I, whenever I was in the recording booth,

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.960
I had to put myself in my shower.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.400
And so I just basically sang
with my back towards the booth,

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:22.290
so that I could feel
totally alone, and sing out.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:25.740
It's, it's not easy and,
and my hat is off to

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:29.340
all performers who, who do
it so effortlessly, you know?

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:32.640
It's, it's not my first, um,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.630
uh, love

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:37.397
and I, I'm not terribly good at it, so...

00:03:37.397 --> 00:03:39.690
- I, I I I'm with you, but I felt like

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.320
the singing was harder for me personally.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:44.400
I, I think in our minds, we all have like

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.110
a five octave range.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.850
And you're, you can just sort
of do anything, but then your

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.890
your, your mouth opens and
you push air through it

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:53.008
and you're like, oh God, that's
a, that's a little reedy.

00:03:53.008 --> 00:03:54.330
(crowd and costars laugh)

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.407
So I struggled with, I
personally struggled with that.

00:03:57.407 --> 00:03:58.327
- What about you?

00:03:58.327 --> 00:03:59.630
- [Octavia And Ryan] Yeah, what about you?

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.730
- I, I think I was like
most comfortable singing and

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.370
in the studio with like, the
headphones on and being like

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.330
can we take that again?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.163
- Yeah.

00:04:07.163 --> 00:04:09.600
- I really enjoyed the, the kind of

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.430
the performance of being a singer.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.873
- [Will] But dance is your
back, part of your background.

00:04:12.873 --> 00:04:14.580
- I do have dance in my background,

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.820
so I was also very excited to,

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.278
to get to put that out there.

00:04:19.278 --> 00:04:20.292
- Kind of show that off?

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:21.775
- A little bit. Yeah.

00:04:21.775 --> 00:04:22.791
- You were a little cocky, during filming,

00:04:22.791 --> 00:04:23.916
- I was a little cocky?

00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:25.296
- I'm just gonna say.

00:04:25.296 --> 00:04:26.797
- I don't remember it like that.

00:04:26.797 --> 00:04:28.629
- To let you know that we
felt you acted cocky at times.

00:04:28.629 --> 00:04:29.462
- We felt this was the right forum.

00:04:29.462 --> 00:04:30.295
- Yeah.

00:04:30.295 --> 00:04:31.128
- [Sunita] Oh no.

00:04:31.128 --> 00:04:31.971
- To tell you,

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:32.804
- Oh, you were all so nice to me

00:04:32.804 --> 00:04:34.829
and I was putting you
down that whole time.

00:04:34.829 --> 00:04:36.664
- But this was the moment
where we thought we

00:04:36.664 --> 00:04:39.226
should let you know our
true feelings about you,

00:04:39.226 --> 00:04:40.970
you know, conceited.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.420
- We got the shot, didn't we?

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.320
- You know what?

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.220
I have to say one thing.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.140
One, the hard, the biggest
challenge for me, was I,

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.450
in all of our singing,
Will and I, for some reason

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.920
were face to face.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.300
Like, they couldn't have us just

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.410
like facing different directions.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.490
We were face to face.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.650
You try singing for like
three weeks straight

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.322
while staring at Will Ferrell.

00:04:57.322 --> 00:04:58.247
(everybody laughs)

00:04:58.247 --> 00:05:01.563
It's like, who's like, you know, like,

00:05:01.563 --> 00:05:04.380
he's like holding his ear for no reason.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.880
And like I would, I would hit a note

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.330
and he'd look at me and go...

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.053
Again.

00:05:13.772 --> 00:05:14.760
- Better. Better.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.593
- Yeah.

00:05:16.866 --> 00:05:17.700
It was so brutal.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:18.533
- [Sunita] So funny.

00:05:18.533 --> 00:05:20.190
You can actually hear me
laughing on the tracks.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.023
I'm sure now.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:22.793
Holding it back.

00:05:22.793 --> 00:05:25.020
- You're all so wonderful
in it and you pull it off

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.820
and you sound amazing and look amazing.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:27.653
- Thank you.

00:05:27.653 --> 00:05:28.743
It's very... yeah

00:05:28.743 --> 00:05:29.667
(crowd cheers)

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:30.500
The best.

